<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42943" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔσπον</span></b> , aor. 2 of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνέπω</span>: only in
		2pl. in the formula <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔσπετε νῦν μοι, Μοῦσαι</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tell</i> me now, ye Muses,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.484
			</span></i>, al.; later <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔσπετε νῦν μοι ὅσοι
				πολυπράγμονές ἐστε σοφισταί</span> Timo <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>. (Prob. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔν-σπ-ετε</span>
				(v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> l. c.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπ-</span> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνι-σπ-εῖν</span>) is the weak form of
				<i>seq[uglide],</i> cf. Lith. <i>sekù</i>
			'say', Lat. <i>in-sece.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
